| NPA Pattern                                     | Use Case                                | Windows User Rights Assignment                     | Windows Local Groups                                | Required Permissions                     | Permission Description                                                                      |
| ----------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Backup Service Account                          | Backup tools reading system data        | Log on as a service, Back up files and directories | Backup Operators                                    | File read, snapshot access               | Allows backup software to read all system files and create snapshots without modifying data |
| Restore Account                                 | Restore files or systems                | Restore files and directories                      | Backup Operators                                    | File restore rights                      | Allows restoring backup data to system locations                                            |
| Monitoring Agent Account                        | Monitoring tools collect system metrics | Log on as a service                                | Performance Monitor Users, Event Log Readers        | Read performance counters and event logs | Enables monitoring platforms to read system metrics and logs                                |
| Security Agent Account                          | Endpoint security agent operations      | Log on as a service                                | Local Administrators (sometimes required)           | Kernel inspection, file scanning         | Allows endpoint security agent to monitor processes and files                               |
| Local Admin Automation Account                  | Automation tools managing servers       | Log on as a service                                | Administrators                                      | Full local admin rights                  | Allows automation systems to install software and manage server configuration               |
| Patch Management Account                        | Automated patch deployment              | Log on as a batch job                              | Administrators                                      | Install updates                          | Enables patch systems to install OS updates and restart services                            |
| Configuration Management Account                | Enforce configuration policies          | Log on as a service                                | Administrators                                      | Remote command execution                 | Allows configuration management tools to update system settings                             |
| Vulnerability Scanner Account                   | Credentialed security scans             | Log on as a batch job                              | Remote Management Users, Event Log Readers          | Read system configuration                | Allows vulnerability scanners to inspect system configuration                               |
| Log Collection Account                          | SIEM log collection                     | Log on as a service                                | Event Log Readers                                   | Read security and system logs            | Enables log forwarding systems to read logs for security analysis                           |
| IIS Application Pool Account (gMSA recommended) | Identity used to run web applications   | Log on as a service                                | IIS_IUSRS                                           | Read app files, connect DB               | Allows IIS application pools to access application resources                                |
| Application Runtime Account                     | Runs Windows services for applications  | Log on as a service                                | None normally                                       | Access application resources             | Allows service-based applications to run under controlled identity                          |
| Scheduled Task Account                          | Runs scheduled automation scripts       | Log on as a batch job                              | None required usually                               | Script execution rights                  | Allows scheduled tasks to execute scripts                                                   |
| Database Application Account                    | Application connecting to SQL Server    | Log on as a service (if service based)             | SQL Server specific roles                           | DB read/write                            | Allows application to interact with database                                                |
| Database Backup Account                         | Backup SQL databases                    | Log on as a service                                | SQL Server backup role                              | DB backup rights                         | Allows database backups without full DB admin privileges                                    |
| Hypervisor Automation Account                   | VM management automation                | Log on as a service                                | Administrators (Hypervisor host)                    | Hypervisor API control                   | Allows infrastructure automation tools to manage VMs                                        |
| Storage Integration Account                     | Backup or monitoring storage            | Log on as a service                                | None                                                | Storage API access                       | Allows tools to interact with storage devices                                               |
| File Transfer Account                           | Automated SFTP or file exchange         | Log on as a service                                | None                                                | File read/write                          | Allows automated file transfers                                                             |
| API Integration Account                         | Machine-to-machine API communication    | None usually                                       | None                                                | API authentication                       | Allows system integration through APIs                                                      |
| Directory Sync Account                          | Identity synchronization                | Log on as a service                                | Account Operators or specific delegated permissions | Directory read/write attributes          | Enables directory synchronization services                                                  |
| Reporting Account                               | Reporting services querying data        | Log on as a batch job                              | None                                                | Data read                                | Allows reporting tools to retrieve data                                                     |
| Certificate Automation Account                  | Automated certificate renewal           | Log on as a service                                | None                                                | Certificate enrollment                   | Allows certificate management systems to renew certificates                                 |
